// para.synced — a synced signal replicating through a **named** node. `alice.synced_signal(…)` is
// `synced_signal(…)` on a node the program opened, so a multi-identity program replicates each
// identity through its own node. The value semantics are unchanged: the same CRDT, the same
// reactive-graph integration, the same explicit `.sync()`.
//
// Under the deterministic broker both replicas share one bus, so they converge exactly as two
// module-level `synced_signal`s do — the sandbox models convergence, not isolation.
// expect: stdout "alice=1"
// expect: stdout "converged a=3 b=3"
// expect: exit 0
use para.{crdt}
use para.{p2p}
use para.synced.{synced_signal}

alice = p2p.open("noeta-p2p-fixture/alice")

a = alice.synced_signal(crdt.gcounter().increment("A", 1), "shared")
echo "alice=${a.get().value()}"

// A signal on the default node, on the same topic — under the broker the two converge.
b = synced_signal(crdt.gcounter().increment("B", 2), "shared")
a.sync()
b.sync()

echo "converged a=${a.get().value()} b=${b.get().value()}"
